<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John II, Count of Holland</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1247–1304</span> · Also known as John II of Avesnes, John II, Count of Hainaut</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John II of Avesnes was count of Hainaut from 1280 and of Holland and Zeeland from 1299 until his death in 1304. A grandson of Countess Margaret II of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flanders">Flanders</a> and Hainaut by her first marriage, he inherited Holland and Zeeland from his young cousin John I. The personal union linked Hainaut with the Dutch-speaking north and continued under his descendants into the fifteenth century.</p></div>
